WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.058
What if your next business website started with a
conversation?

00:00:04.058 --> 00:00:06.087
Welcome to Elevate for Humanity.

00:00:06.087 --> 00:00:08.521
I am PARIS, your AI presenter.

00:00:08.521 --> 00:00:10.956
This episode introduces Elevate's website builder.

00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:16.637
Start by explaining your business, your audience, your
services, and what you want visitors

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:17.449
to do.

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:23.130
Then review a draft, ask for changes, and check the
mobile layout before publishing.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:28.405
Imagine a barber describing haircut services, location,
opening hours, and a booking link.

00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:34.086
A useful first page answers four questions: who are you,
what do you offer,

00:00:34.086 --> 00:00:38.549
where are you, and how can someone take the next step?

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:41.796
Bring your own approved photos and accurate prices.

00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:45.448
Read every AI generated claim before it goes live.

00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:51.129
The store has a public demonstration, while the
authenticated builder is the workspace for

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:53.158
saving and publishing customer websites.

00:00:53.158 --> 00:00:56.404
A demonstration is not your published business site.

00:00:56.404 --> 00:01:02.085
For your first exercise, write one sentence about your
ideal customer and list three

00:01:02.085 --> 00:01:02.491
services.

00:01:02.491 --> 00:01:08.171
Visit Elevate's store, explore the builder, and review
the current plan and hosting terms.

00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:13.852
Follow Elevate on Spotify and share this episode with a
business owner ready to

00:01:13.852 --> 00:01:14.664
be seen.

